        section#about.page-section
            .container.px-4.px-lg-5
                .row.gx-4.gx-lg-5.justify-content-center
                    .col-lg-10
                        h5.text-primary Publisher: Inscripta AI &nbsp;|&nbsp; Version 1.0

                        h2.mt-4 What is NorgAI?
                        p.qs-lead.mt-3 NorgAI is an AI assistant add-in built directly into Microsoft PowerPoint. It reads your uploaded documents&mdash;RFPs, case studies, research reports, product sheets and meeting notes&mdash;and uses them to generate tailored, client-ready presentations from within the PowerPoint task pane.
                        p Every slide NorgAI creates is grounded in your documents and traceable back to its source. No generic content. No manual copy-paste.
                        p.mb-2 #[strong Core capabilities:]
                        ul.qs-intro-list
                            li Generate complete presentations from RFPs and requirements documents
                            li Adapt existing decks for new clients, industries or audiences
                            li Refresh specific slides with current data from uploaded reports
                            li Ask questions about your documents and get cited answers

                        h2.mt-5 Prerequisites
                        .table-responsive
                            table.table.table-bordered.qs-table.mt-3
                                thead
                                    tr
                                        th(scope='col') Requirement
                                        th(scope='col') Detail
                                tbody
                                    tr
                                        td Office version
                                        td Microsoft 365 or Office 2016+ (desktop or web)
                                    tr
                                        td Internet
                                        td Required&mdash;NorgAI is a cloud-connected add-in
                                    tr
                                        td Account
                                        td Create a free account on the NorgAI login page

                        // ── Step 1 ──
                        .qs-step
                            .qs-step-head
                                span.qs-num 1
                                h2 Open the Add-in
                            ol
                                li Open #[strong Microsoft PowerPoint].
                                li On the ribbon, click the #[strong Home] tab.
                                li Locate the #[strong Norg AI Tools] group and click #[strong Norg AI].
                            .qs-note
                                p If you do not see the #[strong Norg AI Tools] group, click #[strong Home] on the ribbon &rarr; #[strong Add-ins] &rarr; search for #[strong NorgAI] &rarr; click #[strong Add]. The button appears in your Home tab after installation.
                            p The NorgAI task pane opens on the right side of the PowerPoint window. After first launch, it opens automatically whenever you open PowerPoint.

                        // ── Step 2 ──
                        .qs-step
                            .qs-step-head
                                span.qs-num 2
                                h2 Sign In
                            p On first launch, the task pane shows the NorgAI sign-in screen.
                            figure.qs-fig
                                img.qs-shot(src='/assets/img/products/norgai/quick-start/Login_page_2.png' alt='NorgAI sign-in screen showing the Login button in the PowerPoint task pane' loading='lazy' decoding='async')
                                figcaption.qs-cap Click the Login button to open the secure authentication dialog.
                            ol
                                li Click #[strong Login].
                                li A secure sign-in dialog opens in a separate popup window.
                                li Enter the email and password provided by your administrator.
                                li If your organisation uses Single Sign-On (SSO), complete authentication on your company&rsquo;s login page when prompted.
                                li The dialog closes automatically once you are authenticated, and the NorgAI home screen loads.
                            .qs-note
                                p Your session persists until you log out. If the session expires, click #[strong Login] to re-authenticate.

                        // ── Step 3 ──
                        .qs-step
                            .qs-step-head
                                span.qs-num 3
                                h2 Create a Project
                            p A #[strong project] is a scoped knowledge space for one client, opportunity or engagement. Each project has its own document library and conversation history.
                            ol
                                li Click the #[strong project dropdown] at the top of the task pane.
                                li Click #[strong Add Project].
                                li Type a project name&mdash;for example, #[em Acme Corp Q3 Proposal] or #[em Digital Transformation RFP].
                                li Click #[strong Create].
                            figure.qs-fig
                                img.qs-shot(src='/assets/img/products/norgai/quick-start/Create_project_2.png' alt='New Project dialog with a name field and a Create button' loading='lazy' decoding='async')
                                figcaption.qs-cap Click the project dropdown, then Add Project. Type a name and click Create.
                            .qs-note
                                p Use one project per client or opportunity. This keeps your AI context focused and your outputs accurate.

                        // ── Step 4 ──
                        .qs-step
                            .qs-step-head
                                span.qs-num 4
                                h2 Upload Documents
                            p With your project active, upload the reference materials NorgAI will use to generate content.
                            ol
                                li Click the #[strong Documents] icon in the toolbar (the library icon below the header).
                                li Drag and drop files onto the upload area, or click #[strong browse files] to select them.
                            p.mb-2 #[strong Supported formats:] &nbsp; .pdf &nbsp; .docx &nbsp; .pptx &nbsp; .xlsx &nbsp; .csv &nbsp; .txt &nbsp; .md
                            figure.qs-fig
                                img.qs-shot(src='/assets/img/products/norgai/quick-start/upload_page_2.png' alt='Document upload area with a drag-and-drop zone and a URL import field' loading='lazy' decoding='async')
                                figcaption.qs-cap The upload area accepts drag-and-drop or file-picker selection. A URL import field below it imports text from any public webpage.
                            .table-responsive
                                table.table.table-bordered.qs-table
                                    thead
                                        tr
                                            th(scope='col') Status
                                            th(scope='col') Meaning
                                    tbody
                                        tr
                                            td Uploading
                                            td File is being transferred
                                        tr
                                            td Parsing
                                            td Content is being read and extracted
                                        tr
                                            td Indexing
                                            td Content is being prepared for AI search
                                        tr
                                            td #[strong Fully Processed]
                                            td File is ready for use
                                        tr
                                            td Failed
                                            td Error during processing&mdash;delete and re-upload
                            figure.qs-fig
                                img.qs-shot(src='/assets/img/products/norgai/quick-start/uploaded_docs_2.png' alt='Document list showing files at Fully Processed status' loading='lazy' decoding='async')
                                figcaption.qs-cap Wait for all key documents to reach Fully Processed before generating content. Files still indexing are not yet available to the AI.
                            .qs-note
                                p #[strong Tip:] Upload the most relevant documents first&mdash;the RFP, the client brief and your strongest case studies.

                        // ── Step 5 ──
                        .qs-step
                            .qs-step-head
                                span.qs-num 5
                                h2 Generate or Adapt a Presentation
                            p Type a plain-language request in the chat field and press #[strong Enter].
                            .table-responsive
                                table.table.table-bordered.qs-table
                                    thead
                                        tr
                                            th(scope='col') Goal
                                            th(scope='col') Example prompt
                                    tbody
                                        tr
                                            td New proposal from an RFP
                                            td #[em &ldquo;Create a 10-slide executive proposal based on the uploaded RFP for a logistics CFO.&rdquo;]
                                        tr
                                            td Adapt an existing deck
                                            td #[em &ldquo;Adapt this deck into a proposal for a mid-market retail banking client focusing on digital payments.&rdquo;]
                                        tr
                                            td Refresh a slide with new data
                                            td #[em &ldquo;Update slide 6 with market sizing from the uploaded research report.&rdquo;]
                                        tr
                                            td Ask a question
                                            td #[em &ldquo;What are the mandatory compliance requirements in this RFP?&rdquo;]
                            h3.mt-4 The Plan Review Workflow
                            p Before NorgAI makes any changes to your presentation, it proposes a #[strong slide-by-slide plan] for your review.
                            figure.qs-fig
                                img.qs-shot(src='/assets/img/products/norgai/quick-start/Plan_2.png' alt='AI-generated slide plan listing each slide with its action type and Approve and Give Feedback buttons' loading='lazy' decoding='async')
                                figcaption.qs-cap The plan lists every output slide with its action type. Click any row to expand it and review the content brief before committing.
                            .table-responsive
                                table.table.table-bordered.qs-table
                                    thead
                                        tr
                                            th(scope='col') Action
                                            th(scope='col') Meaning
                                    tbody
                                        tr
                                            td #[strong NEW]
                                            td A new slide will be created
                                        tr
                                            td #[strong MODIFY]
                                            td An existing slide will be updated
                                        tr
                                            td #[strong KEEP]
                                            td Slide is unchanged
                                        tr
                                            td #[strong REMOVE]
                                            td Slide will be deleted
                            ul
                                li Click #[strong Approve] to apply the plan to your presentation.
                                li Click #[strong Give feedback] to request changes&mdash;describe what you want adjusted and NorgAI revises the plan. Repeat until satisfied.
                            figure.qs-fig
                                img.qs-shot(src='/assets/img/products/norgai/quick-start/Approves_plan.png' alt='Presentation updated after approval, with a Sources panel listing the documents consulted' loading='lazy' decoding='async')
                                figcaption.qs-cap After approval, NorgAI applies the changes and shows a Sources panel listing every document consulted. Click the source count to expand the full attribution list.

                        // ── Step 6 ──
                        .qs-step
                            .qs-step-head
                                span.qs-num 6
                                h2 Modify Individual Slides
                            p To update a specific slide without changing the rest of the deck:
                            ol
                                li Navigate to the target slide in PowerPoint.
                                li Type your instruction in the chat&mdash;for example, #[em &ldquo;Update slide 4 with the latest competitive data from the uploaded report.&rdquo;]
                                li NorgAI proposes an updated slide as a #[strong slide card] in the chat.
                                li Click #[strong Apply] on the card to push the change to your deck, or #[strong Apply All] to apply all pending changes at once.
                            figure.qs-fig
                                img.qs-shot(src='/assets/img/products/norgai/quick-start/Modify_slide_2.png' alt='Slide card showing the proposed slide content with a source count and Apply and Apply All buttons' loading='lazy' decoding='async')
                                figcaption.qs-cap The slide card shows the proposed content. Apply inserts the single slide; Apply All pushes all pending slide updates in one action.
                            .qs-note
                                p Use #[strong Ctrl+Z] in PowerPoint to undo any applied slide.

                        // ── Source Tracing ──
                        h2.mt-5 Source Tracing
                        p Every AI response includes a #[strong Sources] panel showing which documents and web pages informed the output.
                        figure.qs-fig
                            img.qs-shot(src='/assets/img/products/norgai/quick-start/Sources_2.png' alt='Expanded Sources panel showing Sources Used and Also Consulted lists' loading='lazy' decoding='async')
                            figcaption.qs-cap Click the source count (for example, &ldquo;8 sources&rdquo;) to expand the panel.
                        ul
                            li #[strong Sources Used]&mdash;documents directly cited in the output.
                            li #[strong Also Consulted]&mdash;additional sources retrieved but not directly cited.
                            li Click any document source to read the exact passage used. Click any web source to open it in your browser.

                        // ── Key Features ──
                        h2.mt-5 Key Features
                        .table-responsive
                            table.table.table-bordered.qs-table.mt-3
                                thead
                                    tr
                                        th(scope='col') Feature
                                        th(scope='col') Description
                                tbody
                                    tr
                                        td Generate presentation
                                        td Create a full deck from uploaded documents
                                    tr
                                        td Adapt existing deck
                                        td Tailor any presentation to a new client or audience
                                    tr
                                        td Plan Review
                                        td Approve or refine a proposed slide plan before changes apply
                                    tr
                                        td Modify individual slides
                                        td Update specific slides via natural language
                                    tr
                                        td Document Q&amp;A
                                        td Ask questions about uploaded documents and get cited answers
                                    tr
                                        td Source attribution
                                        td Every output is traceable to its source document or web page
                                    tr
                                        td Project knowledge spaces
                                        td Isolated document library and context per project
                                    tr
                                        td Team collaboration
                                        td Share projects with team members
                                    tr
                                        td URL import
                                        td Import text from any public webpage as a document source

                        // ── Support ──
                        h2.mt-5 Support
                        .table-responsive
                            table.table.table-bordered.qs-table.mt-3
                                tbody
                                    tr
                                        td Product website
                                        td
                                            a.text-primary(href='/products/norgai') inscripta.ai/products/norgai
                                    tr
                                        td Full User Guide
                                        td
                                            a.text-primary(href='/products/norgai/user-guide') inscripta.ai/products/norgai/user-guide
                                    tr
                                        td Support &amp; contact
                                        td
                                            a.text-primary(href='/#contact') inscripta.ai/#contact
                                    tr
                                        td Support email
                                        td
                                            a.text-primary(href='mailto:sales@inscripta.ai') sales@inscripta.ai
                                    tr
                                        td Privacy policy
                                        td
                                            a.text-primary(href='/legal/privacy') inscripta.ai/legal/privacy
                                    tr
                                        td Terms of use
                                        td
                                            a.text-primary(href='/legal/norgai-terms') inscripta.ai/legal/norgai-terms

                        .qs-cta
                            p.mb-3 Ready to go deeper? The #[strong Full User Guide] covers every feature&mdash;projects, adaptation, the plan workflow, knowledge &amp; memory, collaboration, troubleshooting and more.
                            a.btn.btn-secondary.btn-lg.mt-1(href='/products/norgai/user-guide')
                                | Read the Full User Guide
                                i.fas.fa-arrow-right.ms-2
                            p.text-muted.small.mt-4 NorgAI is developed by Inscripta AI Technologies Private Limited. For enterprise licensing and administrator setup, contact your account representative.

